      "text": "{\n  \"cautions\": [\n    \"Do not conclude the GPU is dead from XID 79 alone — thermal trips and power droop present identically.\",\n    \"Do not reboot and return the node to the pool without the Redfish check; the fault will recur under load.\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_to_collect\": [\n    \"dmesg Xid lines\",\n    \"Redfish inlet/hotspot temperatures\",\n    \"Redfish PSU redundancy\",\n    \"Redfish PCIe error counters\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"xid-79-bus\",\n  \"keywords\": [\n    \"xid 79\",\n    \"fallen off the bus\",\n    \"pcie\",\n    \"gpu disappeared\",\n    \"nvidia-smi no devices\",\n    \"bus\"\n  ],\n  \"severity\": \"critical\",\n  \"steps\": [\n    \"Confirm the event: grep dmesg for 'Xid 79' and note GPU PCI address, node, and timestamp.\",\n    \"Check Redfish out-of-band telemetry: inlet temperature, GPU hotspot if reported, and PSU redundancy status.\",\n    \"If PSU redundancy is lost or PCIe uncorrectable counters are above zero, treat power delivery as the prime suspect and check input draw vs provisioned capacity before touching the card.\",\n    \"If hotspot is high while inlet is normal (roughly 23-27C), suspect card cooling (heatsink mount, fan zone) rather than the room.\",\n    \"Drain the node so no new work lands on it while diagnosis continues.\",\n    \"If power and thermal look normal, reseat or move the card; if XID 79 persists after reseat, open an RMA/service ticket.\"\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The driver lost PCIe communication with the GPU. In this project's triage experience the cause is more often power delivery or a thermal trip than a dead card, so evidence comes first: in-band tools cannot see the card in this state, which makes out-of-band Redfish telemetry the primary source.\",\n  \"symptoms\": [\n    \"gpu disappeared from nvidia-smi\",\n    \"driver lost the gpu\",\n    \"xid 79 in dmesg\",\n    \"node lost a gpu under load\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"XID 79 — GPU has fallen off the bus\",\n  \"xids\": [\n    79\n  ]\n}"
    }
  ]
}

